  "question": {
    "text": "A particle is moving along a circular path with a constant speed of $10 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}$. What is the magnitude of the change in velocity of the particle, when it moves through an angle of $60^{\\circ}$ around the centre of the circle?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$10 \\sqrt{3} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "zero",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$10 \\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0101_e44a3eecc618.png\"><br>Change in velocity,<br>$$<br>\\begin{array}{l}<br>|\\Delta \\overline{\\mathrm{v}}|=\\sqrt{\\mathrm{v}_{1}^{2}+\\mathrm{v}_{2}^{2}+2 \\mathrm{v}_{1} \\mathrm{v}_{2} \\cos (\\pi-\\theta)} \\\\<br>=2 \\mathrm{v} \\sin \\frac{\\theta}{2} \\quad\\left(\\because\\left|\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{v}}_{1}\\right|=\\left|\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{v}}_{2}\\right|\\right)=\\mathrm{v} \\\\<br>=(2 \\times 10) \\times \\sin \\left(30^{\\circ}\\right)=2 \\times 10 \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\\\<br>=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}<br>\\end{array}<br>$$"
  }
}